WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.390
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.980
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.400
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.820
Things never get any better.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.040
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.510
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.260
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.390
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.150
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.110
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.450
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:22.030
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.540
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.000
This plan isn't very becoming of you.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.100
Of course it isn't!

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.760
If I use the same reasoning that Kaishou has come to expect,

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.720
he'll be able to slip away.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.030
This broadcast is a means for getting him out in the public eye,

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.240
so that he has no chance of talking his way out of it.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.980
Are you that bothered by Kaishou Rinroku?

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.730
I simply want to bring the truth to light.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.530
Have you ever been interested in the truth?

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:03.660
According to Inga, you became a detective for her sake.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.330
That's wrong!

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.790
I became a detective so that I could discover people's truths.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.670
Since it was the only thing I could do.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.550
"People's Truths."

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.690
That's what a soul is, isn't it?

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:18.520
You made a promise to Inga to feed her souls;

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.760
Isn't that why you became a detective?

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.860
With Inga not here,

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.310
isn't there no reason for you to seek out the truth?

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.640
Kaishou is using Bettennou.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:29.890
You think I can just ignore that?

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.150
Well...

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.940
...I agree.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:52.900
This is just one of the simulatory videos that have been floating around the net.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.380
What was it that destroyed the TV station that day?

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:59.630
The most common theory has been that it
was caused by a weapon using microwaves...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.760
Witness, Kaishou Rinroku-kun.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.770
Microwaves, or electromagnetic waves, can't be seen with the naked eye anyway, but...

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:18.760
...the power density of microwave transmissions is 23 milliwatts per square centimetre at most.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.030
This is less than a hundredth of the power of what a domestic microwave employs.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.650
Oh, really?

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.740
According to the documents leaked by Full Circle-

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.540
Ah, and these are genuine, aren't they?

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.920
In these, the experimental value is stated to be several hundred megawatts.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.920
That's nothing close to what a microwave uses, is it?

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.550
That number is a measure of its lifetime durability;

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.920
it doesn't make sense to compare that to its transmission capability.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:44.540
I'm not too clear on the technical aspects, but doesn't this prove,

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:49.260
as many foreign countries have accused, that the technology could be appropriated as a weapon?

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.310
Wait, was JJ Systems a weapons manufacturer?

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.930
In 2001...

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.120
...people witnessed the scene of passenger jets flying into buildings,

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.930
then turned right around and spread rumours of planned explosions.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.820
There were even those who believed such
ridiculous theories as hydrogen bombs being used.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.330
Now, in 2011, the influence of those misfortunes still remain,

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:17.590
creating people who think that natural disasters are all caused by some "earthquake weapon".

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.710
Why is the detective...?

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:24.840
People tend to believe that the truth is something hidden.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:29.850
There are subsequently those who believe they themselves will someday learn it.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.440
But there are an innumerable amounts of truths.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.070
If someone becomes satisfied with a single truth,

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.580
it simply means that they've stopped thinking any further.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.600
At least that's what I believe.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.400
Is he trying to twist the truth with the power of Bettennou?

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.780
I'm not sensing anythi-

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.220
Therefore it's acceptable to hide the truth?

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.410
That's the way you always do things.

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:56.040
Hide? I'm not hiding anything.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.000
That's the Defeated Detective!

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:59.660
A mysterious explosion occurred at the TV station.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.660
What does he think he's doing?

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.440
This is the truth.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:06.470
Also, at the time of the explosion, Kaishou Rinroku was outside the door of the studio and managed to survive.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.680
But is this also true?

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.830
Don't...

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:15.190
What if Mr. Kaishou didn't even come to the TV station in the first place?

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:16.480
What are you saying?!

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:18.600
Kaishou Rie-san...

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.230
...on the day of the explosion, what was it that you saw?

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.050
He's saying Kaishou wasn't there?!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.200
You're acting strange;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.700
I thought this hearing was supposed to prove his innocence.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.950
Rie... Go ahead and tell him.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:33.100
That detective believes in you;

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.560
he believes that you're a girl who cannot lie.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.210
You mustn't betray that trust.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.660
Right after the explosion occurred...

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.970
...I saw... My father at home.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:54.600
What?!

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.580
At home?!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:56.350
What on Earth?!

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.230
But just because he was home, it doesn't mean he had anything to do with the explosion!

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.430
I examined the surveillance footage from the TV station,

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.830
but there was no record of Kaishou Rinroku being there that day.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.870
Could it be the other people involved simply collaborated in saying he was there?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.660
Hey, hey, don't start treating me like an accomplice!

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:19.460
If we consider that it would also be possible to detonate the bomb from a remote location...

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:20.830
Objection! Objection!

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.840
This is not a courtroom.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:30.620
Understood.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:41.520
In the first place, the cause of the explosion is still in the
process of being investigated by the military and the police.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.610
This is unconfirmed,

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.020
but they're rumored to have found
fragments of a surface-to-air missile...

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.780
A missile?!

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:49.640
Oh my! But now that you mention it, back in 2001,

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.070
there was a theory that the Pentagon was destroyed by a missile,

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.080
not a passenger jet!

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.110
We're not talking about a conspiracy theory... The proof is-

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:01.330
It may even be the same type used in the Public
Defense Force's standard-issue rocket launchers.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.080
More than six hundred were supplied to them during the war.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.230
Quite a few, I'd say.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.340
When did she get that information?

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.630
Are you implying that the police have been fabricating evidence?

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.280
Huh?! They did?!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.630
No, they didn't!

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:18.890
I'd like to call one more witness to the stand!

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:31.200
Inga... Why are you here?

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.090
You again?

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.990
Answer my question.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.870
Oh my, you mustn't turn to violence!

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:48.730
People have no choice but to answer what she asks.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.880
Just one question...

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:55.960
Tell me the thing that, while absolutely unforgivable,

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:59.700
you have no choice but to hide.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.610
Tell me...

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.520
Tell me!

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:17.010
Just before the war began,

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.540
the president of JJ Systems at the time, Kaishou Rinroku,

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.240
came to the Public Prosecutor's Office,

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:25.040
offering the services of a certain software.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:32.170
The software was able to alter the
last-date-modified of computer files at will...

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.930
Furthermore, leaving no trace.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:42.190
In other words, it is able to change the creation date of evidence and establish proof of a crime.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.690
Hey, somebody stop her!

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:44.440
Why?

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.200
She's going to leak something important!

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:48.440
Mr. Kaishou was the only one with the software keys.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.440
This information has nothing to do with this committee!

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:56.240
Most of the criminals during the war were apprehended
through his cooperation with the police and prosecutors...

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.190
Hayami-kun?

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.700
You shouldn't involve yourself with Kaishou any longer.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.190
You should consider your position...

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.370
What... What did I say?!

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:09.800
No!

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:27.690
I can't believe it turned out like this... I'm so sorr-

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.950
You, who can't lie, said that I was at home.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:37.710
Therefore,

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:41.700
Yuuki Shinjuurou will certainly infer the presence of Bettennou.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.290
He's a great detective, after all.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.710
Rie... I was at home, wasn't I?

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.400
Inga!

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:19.910
Why did you do that?!

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:23.130
I want to eat souls.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:26.090
But you told me not to kill!

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:31.420
It's too much trouble to eat their souls without killing them.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.880
Are you saying you can't work with me anymore?!

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:57.100
The prosecutors have yet to form a case against that murderer!

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.430
They think they can fool us?!

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:01.660
And it seems they're denying the
existence of that alteration software!

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:04.410
Fuwa-san, we've heard reports that
you met with Mr. Kaishou that day...

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:08.990
Well, yeah, but... He came late and left his seat almost immediately...

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:11.040
Ah, that's right! Kaishou wouldn't have got up like that;

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.290
It may have been a body double!

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.110
That unidentified body that came in yesterday?

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.170
Are you sure you checked everywhere?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.470
I thought I made a mistake and tried everywhere I could think of...

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:20.420
...but I can't find it anywhere!

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.660
Kaishou-san!

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.390
Do you admit to your crimes?!

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:49.120
An illegal program... Murder... What do you have to say for yourself?!

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.180
Kaishou-san, please explain yourself!

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.330
Chairman Kaishou!

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.540
You have an obligation to explain yourself to the public!

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:57.870
I have somewhere I need to stop by.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.020
You should go give our thanks to the doctors.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.700
But Father...

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:04.930
Kaishou-san, please answer us!

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:05.640
Kaishou!

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.060
Kaishou-san, please answer!

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:08.060
What is your relationship with that female prosecutor?!

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.810
Have you finished your backroom deal with the prosecutors?

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.370
This is flooding all over the net,

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.190
along with posts threatening to kill you!

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.310
Kaishou-san, what do you have to say?!

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.070
Mizuno...

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.950
Everyone, please step away!

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.530
The car can't pull out!

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:25.480
Like we give a damn!

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.570
Father...

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:27.820
It's dangerous to stand too close...

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:29.030
Chairman Kaishou!

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:30.060
Kaishou-san!

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.540
Are you running away?!

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.220
Father...?

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:46.210
Whoa, this is bad!

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:46.970
Are they all right?!

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:48.940
Father!

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:49.840
Put out the fire!

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.850
Hey... What's happening?!

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:56.230
Once he knew he couldn't escape, he planned his own suicide, huh?

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.770
The wake has solemnly begun.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:14.120
The effects of the role played by Kaishou
Rinroku in post-war Japan know no bounds...

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.220
If Mr. Kaishou did indeed plan his own suicide,

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.500
the fact that he took his driver, Mizuno Sakon,

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.960
along with him is unforgivable.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:28.010
Haven't you done enough already?!

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:29.640
Defeated Detective!

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.020
Izumi-san!

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:36.850
You bastard...

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.780
...you're the one who killed him!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.900
It was suicide after all?

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:52.990
I don't know!

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:58.230
But the DNA collected from the bodies matched that of Mizuno and Chairman Kaishou!

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:03.000
The ones who killed him... were you and me!

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:07.010
What have I done...?

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:12.390
Wait a second!

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:13.740
Where's Bettennou?

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.150
There's no trace of any such thing!

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:18.450
I know she was there with Kaishou!

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:20.030
Shut the hell up already!

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:21.100
I know she was there...

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:22.230
Please, stop it.

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:24.300
Not here...

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:31.370
When I checked, I found out that all of the data on my father's computer had been erased...

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:33.600
...without a single trace.

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:37.520
That's why I think it may have been suicide.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.080
Was he the kind of man to take Mizuno,

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.380
his bodyguard, along with him?

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.500
What do you know about my father?!

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:50.860
I didn't know anything about him either...

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:53.970
I think I just wanted to understand him...

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:56.200
To know who he truly was,

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.210
and that's why I cooperated with you.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.470
But there was no point in any of it...

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:04.400
No point?

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.440
It's just as my father said:

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.210
There are as many truths as there are people.

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:11.030
Even you...

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.160
What about me?

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:16.690
There are any number of truths about you that you haven't shown me.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:17.720
What does that have to do with-

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:21.290
Just what is that Inga woman to you?

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:25.540
That's... a long story.

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:30.840
It's fine. I have a lot of things that I can't tell you, either.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.850
Father was saying that you would,

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:37.160
"certainly infer the presence of Bettennou".

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.030
Huh?

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:40.740
Oh, some blood...

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.260
What did he mean by that...?

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.020
Once I'm aware of there being two Kaishous,

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:48.300
it would be obvious to infer the presence of Bettennou...?

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.310
Wait!

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:52.650
A handkerchief...

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.160
Pardon me!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:06.850
Milady, I'd like to take this opportunity to say I'm really, really, really sorry for your loss.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:09.830
I only asked him to appear as a witness,

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.420
but this detective started saying all these strange things...

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:14.550
It's okay.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:18.050
Where is it? Where did he leave it?!

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:21.490
If that vehicle explosion wasn't an act of suicide,

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:22.560
the most likely suspects are...

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.630
...Fuwa Juujirou, who survived the first explosion,

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:31.010
Mihara Yasutarou, who became commander of the Public Security Force after the death of Mizuno,

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.200
and that man we saw leaving the hospital...

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:33.200
Here it is!

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.920
How long has that handkerchief been there?

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:37.620
Since when?!

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:42.160
Well... Inga left it there the last time he was here.

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:49.590
But on that same afternoon,

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.670
I gave this handkerchief to Diet Member Kuramitsu Mine.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.380
When did Inga get this?

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:58.740
He's been meeting with Kuramitsu Mine...

00:16:58.740 --> 00:16:59.930
Where?! When?!

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:02.130
Speaking of Diet Member Kuramitsu,

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:03.680
I happen to have found something interesting.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.600
The Public Security Force's Mizuno Sakon,

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:09.310
who died along with Mr. Kaishou,

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:12.940
was her senior in university, and they were apparently close.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.700
It sure didn't seem that way...

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:21.570
Shall I hack into the university's registry?

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:22.910
Hacking...?

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:24.700
Kazamori!

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:28.580
Do you remember what Mizuno said to me when I first met him?

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:31.280
"Defeated Detective!"

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.800
"Are you sure it wasn't you who targeted Kaishou-sensei?"

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.590
Not that! Something he said later!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.620
Ah, that noise is a bonus feature.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.340
Just say it already!

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:44.850
"It seems you managed to succeed for once with Yajima-san's request. But..."

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:46.400
That's it!

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:47.980
That's what's been bothering me.

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:52.110
In the end, no crime had taken place concerning Yajima-san's request.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.190
Therefore it wasn't reported on in the news.

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:57.200
Nonetheless, he knew about it. Why?

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:10.130
What the hell, man?!

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:22.330
You wanna know something about that song?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.880
It's either considerably old, or hasn't been electronically recorded...

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:31.860
Well, it isn't too old of a song... it came out quite recently.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:44.330
It's from that unreleased Yonagahime album.

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:49.660
I really must apologise for what happened last time... What can I say?

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:51.170
For us, it was...

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:52.290
Don't worry about it!

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:55.030
I enjoyed my experience here.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:58.060
'Cause you were surrounded by girls, right?

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:00.830
What could you possibly have to ask him now?

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:03.300
This is a busy time for me to be helping you out.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:07.180
I expect that he knows more about Bettennou than anyone else.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.530
Bettennou?

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:14.310
Are you still thinking that Kaishou Rinroku had Bettennou in his possession?

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:18.320
If he did, making it appear as if he'd died would be a simple task.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.570
Kaishou Rinroku is alive?

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.630
Give it back to me!

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.880
These are all records pertaining to Bettennou...

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:48.890
W-Well, yes, we allow the prisoners to write stories at this facility.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:51.280
Ever since I happened to meet that thing,

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:55.120
I've been repeatedly running experiments and making records of its abilities.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.950
I tried out everything it was capable of.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.880
That's why it belongs to me.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.080
Give it back!

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.290
Hmm?

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:05.280
What's this about "the living and the dead"?

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.570
That's really quite interesting.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:10.660
Say, for instance, there's a living person in this room.

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:16.980
The thing that you refer to as Bettennou would find it difficult to make you believe that person was dead.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:17.670
Why is that?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.190
A living person talks and moves.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:23.200
The brain receives influence from those things through the senses of sight and hearing,

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:28.780
creating unbearable frustration through their contradiction with Bettennou's "story".

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:33.060
For instance, if I tried to make someone believe that I am Yuuki Shinjuurou;

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:36.780
Because you're looking at the real thing already,

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:39.480
your brain wouldn't be able to endure that contradictory information.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:43.190
But if you had the corpse of an explosion victim, with it's general form still intact.

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:49.080
In that case, it would be simple to convince all involved that it was your own corpse.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.360
The necessary part is that they hear your voice.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:56.840
As people's senses are influenced by Bettennou's power, their brains...

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:01.230
I still can't believe it.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:06.990
You're seriously saying that Kaishou Rinoku used Bettennou's power to commit murder and fake his own death?

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:10.140
What's that?

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:14.220
A party invitation that was delivered to my office this morning.

00:21:14.220 --> 00:21:15.750
The sender is...

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:37.500
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:45.470
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:53.140
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:57.440
As if we can see right through it,

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:01.480
We follow it along.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:05.440
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:09.450
Like a falling feather.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:12.580
Looking for, find it,

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:18.920
So we can come closer together.

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:37.430
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:37.430 --> 00:22:41.440
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:44.520
Looking for, find it,

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:49.360
So we can come closer together.

00:22:51.660 --> 00:22:54.190
But the thing called "truth" doesn't really exist.

00:22:54.190 --> 00:22:57.450
Honestly, "truth" is just something that's always being searched out.

00:22:57.450 --> 00:22:59.370
People search for the "truth" for eternity,

00:22:59.370 --> 00:23:01.620
but the "truth" is eternally ephemeral.

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:03.670
The quest for "truth" brings it into existence,

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:07.520
but it is an object through which its existence proves its non-existence.

00:23:07.520 --> 00:23:09.790
When the "truth" occurs in this physical world,

00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:12.490
humans have already ceased to be human, you see.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:14.600
From "I Give Reason".

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:17.850
Next time on UN-GO: "I'm Merely Searching".

00:23:18.470 --> 00:23:21.060
Well, Shinjurou... This is the end.
